+## Interactive invocation mode
+
+New trials run both pinned clients in their actual interactive TUIs. A host `Bun.Terminal`
+connects to `docker exec -it`; neither client uses a print/exec headless mode. The exact task
+prompt is the positional initial prompt. Model/effort, MCP configuration, tools, fixtures,
+request/instruction capture, and deterministic verifiers stay selected by the existing runner.
+The native Codex `exec`-only switches (`--json`, `--ignore-rules`, `--skip-git-repo-check`,
+output-file/stdin flags) and Claude print/stream-json switches are absent. Codex runs its own
+TUI without the shared daemon and with a trusted isolated workspace; Claude receives isolated
+onboarding/theme/workspace preferences. These are declared invocation changes, not evidence
+that the old headless and new interactive system prompts/timings are interchangeable.
+
+Completion is a real persisted native artifact: Codex `task_complete` or Claude's last
+assistant `end_turn` with no outstanding tool result. A quiet screen or an exit code alone is
+not completion. The supervisor then sends the normal Ctrl-D; it sends a second Ctrl-D only
+after the exact `Press Ctrl-D again to exit` UI cue. An unresponsive TUI times out/fails and is
+reaped rather than being reported as clean. Only the exact custom-key confirmation for the
+runner-owned isolated loopback gateway token has a configured startup reply; unrelated auth
+and permission prompts are never auto-accepted.
+
+Each private trial retains `terminal.raw`, timestamped `terminal-events.jsonl`, rendered
+`terminal-screen.txt`, `interactive-session.json`, and the genuine native transcript. The
+`events.jsonl` receipt is copied byte-for-byte from that transcript; it is not fabricated
+`stream-json` output. `control/final.txt` comes from the actual native final message. Existing
+wire captures remain unchanged and authoritative for partial delivery and upstream timing.
+`duration_ms` ends when native completion is observed; terminal shutdown time is separately
+recorded in `interactive.exitDurationMs`.
+
+Manifests declare `invocation_mode=interactive-pty-v1`, terminal profile/runtime, completion
+and event sources, adapter source hashes and dependency-lock hash. Comparison rejects a mix
+of historical headless and interactive receipts or incompatible adapters. Resume refuses
+historical headless runs. Preserve those receipts and use a fresh label; do not pool them.
+
+The original bypass permission controls are explicitly declared as `permission_profile`.
+Known session-title generations are labeled separately only when the request has the
+`structured_output` JSON schema with sole string property `title` and the developer naming
+instruction. Original requests and all channel statistics remain retained; additional
+`request_phases`, task-generation counts and auxiliary model/effort differences prevent a
+title-generation setting from being mistaken for the task's setting. Unknown requests are
+not silently reclassified. This reporter profile is separately versioned and hash-pinned;
+the frozen wire capture and historical delivery analyzer are not rewritten.
+
+Model-free adapter validation (no model/native AI client is started):
+
+```sh
+bun test tools/agent-bench/interactive-pty.test.ts tools/agent-bench/interactive-clients.test.ts
+BENCH_PTY_DOCKER_IMAGE=sha256:e8901954c57c01248173bc31abb918d3a557adf768b9508060e3442db7ff56a3 \
+  bun test tools/agent-bench/interactive-docker.test.ts
+```
+
+The Docker test uses the already-loaded pinned runner image with networking disabled; it
+does not pull/rebuild an image, mount credentials, or modify task verifiers. Real-client
+probe/paid evaluation still requires the user's explicit GO; model-free tests do not claim
+to prove pinned-client startup/exit behavior on a model-backed turn.
